{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Round 2 complete (~$90/$150 cumulative). (1) Sonnet-as-Opus frontier swap: NOT viable as configured — 0/3 hard-ticket replays completed (Bedrock-Sonnet web-search tool errors abort runs on T1; agentic finders burn full 125-request budgets at ~$15-20/ticket, echoing the recorded 'sonnet fan-out false economy' finding). Nova Pro: 8/8 verdict agreement incl. a 12-child container epic and two blocking-heavy tickets at ~$0.10/run, but blocking-criteria recall only ~50-57% (verdict-safe, finding-lossy). p99 giant tickets are no longer replayable — today's desc-cap gate 7cf80009d9 DET-blocks that class pre-LLM. (2) CV 6/22 answered: harness artifact of the experiment runner (verifier searched the real repo, not the fixture); fixture-rooted Sonnet = 22/22, no prompt remediation needed. Ranking: Sonnet 22/22 > Haiku 19/22 (0 false-accepts, over-strict from shallow search; ~$0.75/run vs $2.24 cache-aware) > Nova 2 Lite 14/22 > Nova Pro 13/22 with 3 false-accepts (disqualified). Haiku window: ~6% of calls / 18% of completion spend would exceed 200k peak and ladder back to Sonnet. (3) Loop audit: overlap-judge fix 7fa8102477 bounded judge_batch but NOT judge_one (volume site) — extend the same 3 bounds there (~97% failure-cost cut); CV runaways fixed into bounded budget-exhaustions still costing $20-30/day — next lever is a cumulative-cost ceiling per attempt. Pricing note: pydantic-ai input_tokens is cache-inclusive and Opus 4.8 is $5/$25 — all round-1 report figures stand; round-1 experiment-spend table was overstated (true ~$13). Data: reports/llm-gate-cost-2026-08-11/round2/."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786469063267107001,"uuid":"3f975c15-26c5-434a-8563-c6b48b32936c"}